@startuml GitEasyToolingAudit
title GitEasy - Jargon Audit Tool Sequence (v1.5.5)\ntools/Audit-PublicJargon.ps1
skinparam shadowing false

actor User as U
participant "Audit-PublicJargon.ps1" as Audit
participant "PS Language.Parser\n(AST)" as AST
participant "Test-StringIsUserFacing" as SF
participant "Test-JargonInText" as JT

U -> Audit : .\\tools\\Audit-PublicJargon.ps1 [-ProjectRoot <path>]

Audit -> Audit : validate ProjectRoot and Public\\ exist;\nload HARD + SOFT jargon vocabulary

loop for each Public\\*.ps1 file
  Audit -> AST : ParseFile(path) -> AST + tokens
  AST --> Audit : abstract syntax tree

  loop for each StringConstantExpressionAst node
    Audit -> SF : is this node user-facing?\n(parent = Write-Host/Warning/Error\nor a throw statement?)
    SF --> Audit : $true / $false

    alt string is user-facing
      Audit -> JT : scan for HARD jargon\n(upstream, HEAD, rebase, stash, ...)
      JT --> Audit : matched terms or empty
      Audit -> JT : scan for SOFT jargon\n(commit, push, branch, merge, ...)
      JT --> Audit : matched terms or empty
    end
  end
end

Audit -> U : print findings grouped by file;\nHARD flagged for mandatory fix,\nSOFT flagged for contextual review

note right of Audit
  Read-only. Never modifies any file.\nExit 0 even when findings exist;\ncaller decides how to gate on results.
end note
@enduml
